      "value": "Dont even need to modify the sdk to bypass the poly limit. can have a cube with 12 polys or less with crashes on it just not how these work and the way vrchat work they dont really have a server as such they use like unity's network to connect to other people not everyone connecting to a server etc kinda very basic way of explaining it but you get the idea. in terms of poly count sure millions of poly might affect a PC that's not really good but say a 300k avatar in a room that has no dynamic bones, cloth a few unique materials you wouldn't even notice. i know a few model that are way under the poly limit but because of bones, collides, cloth and animations and such lag the hell out of me there the killers but that also because of the game its very not optimized bones for example use cpu a lot cos its old script. until they switch to unity 2018 unfortunately wont really see much of an improvement if at all the way this is going.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
